# App Shell UI Spec

**Read the full specs before building or refactoring webapp screens:**
- Interaction: [`specs/app-shell-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/app-shell-spec.md)
- Feature catalog: [`docs/reference/ui-architecture-reference.md`](../../docs/reference/ui-architecture-reference.md)
- Visual design: [`specs/design-language-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/design-language-spec.md)
- Data loading: [`specs/data-loading-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/data-loading-spec.md)

## Core invariants

1. **Shell:** sidebar + header (school, year/period, lang, user menu) + body + overlay drawer + modals + toasts.
2. **List page:** title/description top-left; primary CTA + search + filter + more menu top-right; table or cards; row `···` menu on every row; URL-backed detail via `[[id]]` for **complex** entities only.
3. **Detail drawer (complex entities)** — read-only; **entity header** (identity + up to 2 primary actions → modals); body = related content via **sections**, **tabs**, or **both**; no global Save on the shell.
4. **Simple entities (§3.5)** — no drawer; row `···` menu → modals. Row click must not open an empty detail surface.
5. **All mutations use modals** — create (list CTA), edit (entity-header or row `···`), delete (confirm modal), sub-collection add/edit (tab `+ Add` / row Edit).
6. **Pragmatic toggles only** — boolean/single-value flips (permission cell, status chip) may toggle inline with immediate save + toast. Multi-field edits always use a modal.
7. **Complex entities** — body tabs when justified; sub-collection tabs are mini read-only lists; their add/edit always opens a modal.
8. **States** — wrap lists in `DataState`; toast on mutation success/error.

## Do not

- Render `*Form.svelte` as the default drawer body
- Put Save/Cancel on the drawer shell
- Open a drawer that only repeats list-row columns
- Inline-edit sub-collection rows

## Naming

- `<Entity>View.svelte` — list
- `<Entity>Detail.svelte` or `<Entity>Tabs.svelte` — read-only drawer
- `<Entity>FormModal.svelte` — create/edit modal
